-- pending: #669 E1 (a task that outlives each lend, lent the owner afresh at each resume)
-- now: 31:11: the body of `with spawn` assigns a `let mut` variable declared outside it, or lends a place declared outside it: a control handler's body may be abandoned, and does not hand them back; bind what the block answers instead
-- Hard problem 6: two tasks in the scheduler's hands each hold a `mut` borrow of `main`'s tally,
-- and `main` reads the tally between their turns. Each task needs the borrow only while it runs:
-- the lend must end at each `await` and be made again, at a fresh lifetime, when the scheduler
-- resumes the task. The tasks outlive every one of those lends, and the owner is outside them.
--
-- Issue: #669's E1 (H2 (b) at a queue: `NuOk` admits an observation `forall 'b. mut 'b T -o …`),
-- #682. The same shape at a capability is `corpus/pending/io-two-tasks.bc` (SPEC §34 *Open*).
--
-- Rust: refused as written (two live `&mut tally`, and `main` reads it while they are held);
-- Rust's answers are `Rc<Cell<i32>>`, or a coroutine whose resume argument is the `&mut i32`
-- (`Coroutine<&mut i32>`), lent at each `resume`.
--
-- Today: refused at the first `with spawn`: a control handler's body may be abandoned, so it may
-- not lend a place declared outside it. Both backends stop at the same message.
--
-- Once it lands: i32[112233]: the tally read by `main` after the spawns (1 + 10 = 11) and after
-- each of two rounds (22, 33); then both tasks are cancelled; `live 0`.

include async

-- Adds `step` to the tally, then lets the other tasks run, `n` times.
fn ticker<'t>(t: mut 't i32, step: i32, n: i32) -> i32 with Async =
  for i in 0..n { modify t { x -> x + step }; await() };
  n

main -> i32 =
  let mut tally = 0;
  let a = with spawn { ticker(&mut tally, 1, 3) };
  let b = with spawn { ticker(&mut tally, 10, 3) };
  let mut trace = tally;
  match resume(a) {
    inr a -> match resume(b) {
      inr b ->
        trace = trace * 100 + tally;
        match resume(a) {
          inr a -> match resume(b) {
            inr b -> trace = trace * 100 + tally; cancel(a); cancel(b); trace
          | inl v -> cancel(a); 0 - 4 }
        | inl v -> cancel(b); 0 - 3 }
    | inl v -> cancel(a); 0 - 2 }
  | inl v -> cancel(b); 0 - 1 }
